#: ../../../cmds/fish_user_key_bindings.rst:7
msgid "fish_user_key_bindings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cmds/fish_user_key_bindings.rst:12
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cmds/fish_user_key_bindings.rst:14
msgid ""
"``fish_user_key_bindings`` is called automatically whenever fish sets up "
"the :ref:`key bindings <custom-bindings>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cmds/fish_user_key_bindings.rst:16
msgid "That allows you to use it as a simple customization point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cmds/fish_user_key_bindings.rst:18
msgid ""
"Historically, fish could not remember which bindings were defined by a "
"preset like :doc:`fish_default_key_bindings <fish_default_key_bindings>` or "
"by custom configuration, so ``fish_user_key_bindings`` was the only way to "
"add custom bindings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cmds/fish_user_key_bindings.rst:20
msgid ""
"That hasn't been necessary for a while but it stays around because it makes "
"for easy organization - just keep all bindings here to have them in one spot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cmds/fish_user_key_bindings.rst:22
msgid ""
"Adding :doc:`bind <bind>` invocations anywhere in :ref:`config.fish "
"<configuration>` works too, so which you use is a question of taste."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cmds/fish_user_key_bindings.rst:25
msgid "Examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cmds/fish_user_key_bindings.rst:29
msgid ""
"function fish_user_key_bindings\n"
"    # I like the old feature of leaving a ^C marker on ctrl-c\n"
"    bind ctrl-c cancel-commandline\n"
"end"
msgstr ""
